    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** (77.42) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) headline the lineup as our most potent assets. **Kyle Tucker** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Robert Gasser, whose 5.63 xERA is the most exploitable figure on the board, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a favorable platoon edge against Grant Holmes. The data also favors **Andy Pages** (67.85) in that same contest against Robert Gasser; his high SP skill projection and mid-order placement make him a core contributor today. While **Gunnar Henderson** (64.95) faces the difficult Framber Valdez, he remains a mandatory start due to his elite offensive floor and the potential for a stolen base against a pitcher known for a deliberate delivery.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involves **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (51.90), who hit the bench today primarily due to the daunting task of facing Paul Skenes. Despite **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** having a strong base projection, the 19% penalty applied for Skenes\u2019 elite stuff suppressed his score below our threshold, allowing the system to favor the higher-upside matchups for **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) and **Josh Jung** (64.46). Meanwhile, **Coby Mayo** (57.75) and **Gage Workman** (58.70) are currently tracking as marginal starts; their value is buoyed significantly by favorable park factors, but they remain high-variance plays given their lower spots in the order. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that every single slot is subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status, which forces a reliance on historical placement assumptions. We are monitoring the weather closely, though the wind blowing out for **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** provides a slight power boost to their otherwise neutral matchups against Adrian Houser. Users should be aware that **Liam Hicks** (49.64) is at the bottom of the startable range; he is kept in the lineup solely for positional necessity, as any late-breaking news regarding his spot in the order could push him into the bench category to preserve game caps.",
